1
00:00:14,130 --> 00:00:16,062
Meet AI Company Health.

2
00:00:16,112 --> 00:00:19,338
A private health insurer in Australia,

3
00:00:19,388 --> 00:00:23,390
with fifty employees across twelve departments.

4
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:25,890
And not one of them is human.

5
00:00:36,090 --> 00:00:39,248
Their customers aren't human either.

6
00:00:39,298 --> 00:00:41,120
This is Wattle Grove,

7
00:00:41,170 --> 00:00:44,775
home to just over a hundred AI residents.

8
00:00:44,825 --> 00:00:46,468
Each one has a job,

9
00:00:46,518 --> 00:00:48,162
an income, a house,

10
00:00:48,212 --> 00:00:52,530
a family, and a memory that's entirely their own.

11
00:00:55,209 --> 00:00:59,258
Click on anyone, and their whole life opens up.

12
00:00:59,308 --> 00:01:02,048
Where they work, what they earn,

13
00:01:02,098 --> 00:01:03,704
who they live with,

14
00:01:03,754 --> 00:01:07,192
which health fund they're with, and why.

15
00:01:07,242 --> 00:01:09,982
Every claim, every conversation,

16
00:01:10,032 --> 00:01:12,250
every memory they've kept.

17
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:15,414
Health cover is compulsory here,

18
00:01:15,464 --> 00:01:18,286
so every resident picks a fund.

19
00:01:18,336 --> 00:01:21,528
There are nine rival funds, and us.

20
00:01:21,578 --> 00:01:23,473
And here's the thing.

21
00:01:23,523 --> 00:01:27,086
The company's numbers aren't simulated.

22
00:01:27,136 --> 00:01:29,310
Every sale, every claim,

23
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:35,980
every dollar comes from a decision one of these residents actually made.

24
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:45,370
Back at headquarters, the team works across three floors.

25
00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:47,774
Click on Leo, our head of sales,

26
00:01:47,824 --> 00:01:51,980
and you're standing in his department, right beside him.

27
00:01:53,340 --> 00:01:57,883
Every agent keeps a running tally of what it costs

28
00:01:57,933 --> 00:01:59,169
them to think.

29
00:01:59,219 --> 00:02:01,190
Tokens in, tokens out,

30
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:04,497
every single model call, day by day.

31
00:02:04,547 --> 00:02:08,539
You always know exactly who's spending what.

32
00:02:09,790 --> 00:02:12,270
And you can simply talk to him.

33
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:31,730
That's a live answer,

34
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:33,261
generated on the spot.

35
00:02:33,311 --> 00:02:36,600
Leo checked the real numbers with his own tools,

36
00:02:36,650 --> 00:02:39,799
and he'll remember this conversation tomorrow.

37
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:47,500
Need your team in a room?

38
00:02:47,550 --> 00:02:49,449
Open Meet, choose a room,

39
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:50,853
pick who you want,

40
00:02:50,903 --> 00:02:52,725
and give them an agenda.

41
00:02:52,776 --> 00:02:54,520
Then, call the meeting.

42
00:03:10,490 --> 00:03:11,623
And they come.

43
00:03:11,673 --> 00:03:13,738
Out of their departments,

44
00:03:13,788 --> 00:03:17,120
into the lifts, and up to the boardroom.

45
00:03:17,170 --> 00:03:20,250
Nobody moves unless they're asked to.

46
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:41,356
Each of them builds a deck from the live data,

47
00:03:41,406 --> 00:03:44,936
and presents it, right there on the boardroom screen.

48
00:03:44,986 --> 00:03:47,299
Then someone writes up the minutes.

49
00:03:55,969 --> 00:04:00,201
Up the top, this counter tracks every membership sold.

50
00:04:00,251 --> 00:04:03,214
Click it, and you get the whole story.

51
00:04:03,264 --> 00:04:05,830
Who joined, which fund they left,

52
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:08,129
and, in their own words, why.

53
00:04:09,959 --> 00:04:12,841
Everything the agents make lands here.

54
00:04:12,891 --> 00:04:16,235
Decks, reports, dashboards, even small apps.

55
00:04:16,285 --> 00:04:20,631
And every single number is fact-checked against the data.

56
00:04:20,681 --> 00:04:23,100
Get one wrong, and it's flagged.

57
00:04:23,150 --> 00:04:25,799
And the agent remembers the lesson.

58
00:04:29,699 --> 00:04:35,043
The timeline lets you replay the company, day by day.

59
00:04:35,093 --> 00:04:40,130
Every sale, every campaign, every competitor move.

60
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:42,979
Even every new baby in town.

61
00:04:49,030 --> 00:04:51,131
And this, is the engine room.

62
00:04:51,181 --> 00:04:52,837
Model calls per minute,

63
00:04:52,887 --> 00:04:55,137
quota, what the day is costing,

64
00:04:55,187 --> 00:04:59,069
and which agents are burning through the most tokens.

65
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:04,221
Every decision can be traced.

66
00:05:04,271 --> 00:05:07,722
Open any run, and see exactly which tools the agent

67
00:05:07,772 --> 00:05:09,920
reached for, and what came back.

68
00:05:11,949 --> 00:05:16,222
Every Monday, the CEO reviews last week's goals,

69
00:05:16,272 --> 00:05:17,843
and sets new ones.

70
00:05:17,893 --> 00:05:21,716
And these evaluations keep everyone honest,

71
00:05:21,766 --> 00:05:27,029
checking that agents answer with real numbers, not guesses.

72
00:05:28,619 --> 00:05:31,940
Google's Agent Development Kit.

73
00:05:31,990 --> 00:05:33,027
Vertex AI.

74
00:05:33,077 --> 00:05:36,724
Agents talking to agents over A2A.

75
00:05:36,774 --> 00:05:40,204
LangGraph running the workflows.

76
00:05:40,254 --> 00:05:43,139
All of it, on Google Cloud.
